  "query_preview": "/Monday through Friday/...\nUpper-level ridging will build over the western CONUS early\nnext week, returning dry conditions. Through the midweek, a \nweak upper- level shortwave will move onshore and through\nthe Great Basin, although impacts are expected to be minimal. \nGreater impacts are expected late week when another system\nmoves into the Pacific Northwest. Precipitation chances \ncurrently reflect some disagreement when the system will move \nin, but precipitation chances of 10-30% are currently forecast. \nTemperatures will cool slightly at higher elevations while \nholding nearly steady at lower elevations. Winds will generally \nbe light through the week with patchy fog expected in valleys.",
